{
  "title": "🪣 Frustum of a Cone — The Bucket Shape",
  "hook": "Cut off the top of a cone with a slice parallel to the base — the piece left at the bottom is called a 'frustum.' It's the shape of a bucket, a lampshade, or a drinking glass!",
  "explanation": "<div style=\"background:#F3E5F5;border-left:4px solid #7B1FA2;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0\"><strong style=\"color:#7B1FA2\">Frustum:</strong> The portion of a cone between the base and a plane parallel to the base that cuts the cone.</div><div style=\"text-align:center;margin:10px 0\"><svg width=\"200\" height=\"160\"><polygon points=\"50,20 150,20 180,140 20,140\" fill=\"#FFF3E0\" stroke=\"#E65100\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"20\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#E65100\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"80\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#E65100\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"85\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">h</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10\">r</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10\">R</text><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#1565C0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4\"/><text x=\"175\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1565C0\">l</text></svg></div><div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E3F2FD,#BBDEFB);border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1.05rem;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-size:0.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:#1565C0;margin-bottom:4px\">Frustum slant height</div><strong>Slant height: l = √[h² + (R − r)²]</strong></div><div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E3F2FD,#BBDEFB);border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1.05rem;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-size:0.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:#1565C0;margin-bottom:4px\">Frustum volume</div><strong>Volume = (πh/3)(R² + r² + Rr)</strong></div><div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E3F2FD,#BBDEFB);border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1.05rem;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-size:0.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:#1565C0;margin-bottom:4px\">Frustum curved surface</div><strong>CSA = π(R + r)l</strong></div><div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E3F2FD,#BBDEFB);border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1.05rem;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-size:0.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:#1565C0;margin-bottom:4px\">Frustum total surface area</div><strong>TSA = π(R + r)l + πR² + πr²</strong></div><div style=\"background:#FFF8E1;border-left:4px solid #FFB300;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> Memory trick: Frustum volume formula has R² + r² + Rr — it's like the 'average' of all possible pairs of the two radii.</div>",
  "worked_example": "<b>Example:</b> A bucket is in the form of a frustum with top radius 20 cm, bottom radius 10 cm, and height 30 cm. Find its capacity (volume).<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Use frustum volume formula</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">V = (πh/3)(R² + r² + Rr)</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Substitute</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">= (π × 30/3)(400 + 100 + 200)</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Compute</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">= 10π × 700 = 7000π ≈ 21,991 cm³ ≈ 22 litres</span></div></div></div>",
  "try_this": {
    "question": "A flower pot is a frustum with top radius 14 cm, bottom radius 7 cm, height 24 cm. Find the slant height and curved surface area.",
    "hint": "l = √(h² + (R−r)²) = √(576 + 49). CSA = π(R+r)l.",
    "answer": "l = √(576 + 49) = √625 = 25 cm. CSA = π(14+7)(25) = 22/7 × 21 × 25 = 1650 cm²."
  },
  "fun_fact": "The word 'frustum' comes from Latin 'frustum' meaning 'a morsel cut off.' Mathematically, it's always about cutting a cone!"
}